Interface Intent: Genome Browser UI
Purpose
Define the visual structure, layout, and interaction patterns for the web-based genome browser interface that enables exploration of ancient and modern human DNA with population genetic measures.

File Scope
genome_browser.html – DOM structure and semantic markup
genome_browser.css – Visual styling, layout, responsiveness, and theme


Layout Structure
Top Navigation Bar (30px height, 25% width)

Fixed horizontal bar containing:
Browser logo (left-aligned)
Action buttons: population selection, query input, settings
Scrolls with page content
Positioned at top-left of viewport
Annotation Track: anno_mini (30px height, 75% width)

Complements top bar to fill remaining width
Shows simplified chromosome-wide view:
Simplified gene blocks (no exon detail)
Coordinate labels at top, scaled to zoom level
Adaptive tick marks (bp/kb/Mb based on zoom)
Contains semi-transparent focal window (50% opacity fixed)
Scrolls with page content
Annotation Track: anno_full (below anno_mini)

Shows detailed genomic region:
Full gene structures with exons, introns, strand direction
Gene names when space permits
Coordinate ruler at bottom with base-pair resolution at high zoom (<10kb)
Center position synchronized with focal window center in anno_mini
Focal Window Behavior
Visual Properties

Semi-transparent overlay (50% opacity, fixed)
Resizable by dragging edges
Visual handles appear on mouseover of edges
No size constraints (can be any % of anno_mini width)
Interaction Methods

Reposition: Click anywhere on anno_mini outside focal window → window jumps to click position
Resize: Drag edges when handles visible
Define new region: Click + drag on anno_mini to draw new focal window
Synchronization

Focal window position/size always reflects anno_full viewport
Dragging anno_full view → focal window auto-slides in anno_mini
Window boundaries define the genomic region displayed in anno_full
Zoom Interactions
Universal Zoom Behavior

All annotation tracks render together synchronously (anno_mini + anno_full + all population tracks)
Mouse wheel scroll: 2x zoom factor per tick
Double-click: zoom 2x centered on click position
Zoom buttons: standard zoom in/out controls
Coordinate Scale Adaptation

anno_mini: Coordinate labels scale dynamically (show Mb at chromosome scale, kb at gene scale)
anno_full: Always shows highest resolution appropriate for zoom level
At <10kb span: display base-pair resolution coordinates
Pan Interactions
Dragging on anno_mini

Moves the focal window along the chromosome
Does NOT pan the entire chromosome view
anno_full updates to show region defined by new focal window position
Dragging on anno_full

Pans the detailed genomic view left/right
Focal window in anno_mini auto-slides to match
When dragged to edge, focal window continues sliding
Click Navigation

Click outside focal window on anno_mini: focal window jumps to clicked position
Detailed view (anno_full) re-centers on new focal position
Technical Requirements
State Synchronization

Single source of truth: genomic coordinates {chr, start, end}
anno_mini focal window derives position from {start, end} relative to chromosome length
All tracks (anno_mini, anno_full, population tracks) subscribe to same state
Any zoom/pan action updates central state → triggers re-render of all tracks
Rendering Rules

anno_mini: Simplified gene blocks only (rectangles, no exon subdivision)
anno_full: Full gene detail (exons as thick bars, introns as thin lines with strand arrows)
Both tracks maintain consistent color coding (strand + vs -)
Coordinate labels auto-format based on scale (bp, kb, Mb)



C. Population Tracks Section

Section Header (above all tracks):
- Measure selector: Dropdown for choosing genetic measure (FST, heterozygosity, Tajima's D)
- Window size selector: Dropdown (per-SNP, 100kb, 500kb, 1Mb, 5Mb)
- Sort by selector: Dropdown for explanatory variables (age, latitude, longitude, distance from Africa, climate PC1/PC2)
- Export button: Downloads visible data as CSV

Track Layout:
- One track per selected population
- Height: 80px per track (configurable)
- Left margin: Population name/code (e.g., "CEU", "YRI")
- Right margin: Shared Y-axis with measure title and tick labels
- Main area: Line plot aligned with genomic coordinates from ruler above
- Color: Unique per population (from predefined palette)
- Ordering: Sorted by selected explanatory variable

Shared Y-Axis:
- Tick marks and labels shared across all tracks
- Range: Auto-scaled to genome coordinates and annotation tracks

Track Interaction:
- Hover shows tooltip with exact value, position, population name
- Drag-and-drop track reordering by population name
- Synchronized pan/zoom with ruler and annotations
- No per-track status indicators

3. Population Selection Modal
Overlay dialog triggered by population selector button.

Structure:
Search/filter bar at top
Scrollable list of populations with checkboxes
Selection counter: "X of 20 selected"
Ancient DNA section (when applicable):
Radio buttons: Genetic similarity / Geographic distance
Slider or dropdown for threshold value
Genetic similarity: 0-100% (5% steps)
Geographic distance: 10-100,000 km (log scale)
Time distribution chart: Shows sample availability across time
Time range selector: Dual-handle slider for date range
Action buttons: Apply, Cancel
Behavior:

Selections persist during session
Apply closes modal and triggers data fetch
Limit enforced: maximum 20 populations
4. Loading/Status Indicator
Position: Overlay or top bar
States:
Loading data
Computing (with progress if available)
Error message
Job polling status (for async requests)

Visual Design Requirements
Color Palette
Background: Light neutral (#f5f5f5)
Panels: White (#ffffff)
Borders: Subtle gray (#d0d0d0)
Primary action: Blue (#2196F3)
Population tracks: Distinct colors from qualitative palette (colorblind-safe)
Annotations: Muted colors (genes: #7986CB, exons: #5C6BC0)

Typography
Headers: Sans-serif, 16-18px, medium weight
Labels: 12-14px, regular weight
Monospace: For coordinates and numeric values

Spacing
Control bar padding: 12px vertical, 16px horizontal
Track margins: 4px between tracks
Modal padding: 24px

Responsive Breakpoints
Desktop: ≥1024px (full layout)
Tablet: 768-1023px (simplified controls)
Mobile: <768px (stacked controls, modal fullscreen)
Interaction Patterns

Navigation
Pan: Click-drag on ruler or tracks, arrow keys
Zoom: Buttons, scroll wheel (with modifier key), pinch on touch
Jump: Enter coordinates or gene name in query box

Track Management
Reorder: Drag track headers
Highlight: Click to select/focus
Export: Generates CSV of visible region data

Modals
Open: Button click, keyboard shortcut
Close: Apply/Cancel button, Esc key, click outside
Focus trap: Tab cycles within modal when open

Accessibility
Semantic HTML: Proper heading hierarchy, ARIA labels
Keyboard navigation: All functions accessible without mouse
Screen reader: Descriptive labels for all controls and data points
Contrast: WCAG AA compliance minimum
Focus indicators: Visible outlines on interactive elements
Default State

On initial load:
Region: chr1:1,000,000-2,000,000
Measure: FST (or first available)
Window size: 1Mb
Sort by: None (alphabetical by population)
Populations: None selected (user must choose)
Annotation track: Visible with genes/exons loaded

Performance Considerations
Lazy render: Only visible tracks and viewport region
Debounce: Pan/zoom events throttled to 60fps
Canvas rendering: For data tracks when point count >1000
Progressive enhancement: Works without JavaScript for basic structure


MVP Phase 1 - Interface Focus:

Priority 1: Core Navigation
- Region query input (chr:start-end format)
- Zoom in/out controls
- Pan functionality (click-drag)
- Coordinate ruler with dynamic updates
- Default region: chr1:1,000,000-2,000,000

Priority 2: Annotation Display
- GTF loading from S3
- Gene bodies rendering
- Exon/intron visual distinction
- Gene labels at appropriate zoom

Priority 3: Population Selection
- Population selector modal with checkboxes
- Limit: 20 populations maximum
- Search/filter capability
- Selection persistence during session
- NO ancient DNA filtering in MVP

Priority 4: Heterozygosity Visualization
- Single measure selector (heterozygosity only for MVP)
- Window size selector: per-SNP, 100kb, 500kb, 1Mb, 5Mb
- Population tracks: one per selected population
- Shared Y-axis on right with measure title
- Track ordering by population name (alphabetical initially)
- NO sorting by explanatory variables in MVP

Priority 5: Track Interaction
- Hover tooltips showing value, position, population
- CSV export of visible data
- Synchronized pan/zoom across all tracks

Deferred to Later Phases:
- FST and other pairwise measures
- Tajima's D and additional population-level measures
- Sorting by explanatory variables (age, lat, long, etc.)
- Ancient DNA time/similarity filtering
- Track drag-and-drop reordering
